<p>I want to say few things that I (and maybe I alone) finds intriguing.</p>
<p>First, no one ever said that the monthly termination doesn't exist even if the skip said so. Who are you to say that the effect of the memetics is to make every infected person cannot perceive the monthly termination rule? What if <em>the skips itself is the memetics made to make us believe that monthly termination is wrong?</em> I'd say the author is exploring a pretty wild idea here.</p>
<p>Second, just because it was memetics, doesn't instantly stop everyone in the foundation from doing it, and it just make it even more interesting. The infected personnel, or even site, would still faithfully carry out the order and file a report about it, demoted into D-class, and another would get infected and cull them, rinse and repeat.</p>
<p>Third, this is something new. The Foundation ate Infohazards, Cognitohazards and Memetics for breakfast, but just like that one about IDAS, this is something that threaten the unity of the Foundation, hard to contain, but had little to none concern for normal people.</p>

