			<div class="content" id="post-content-2659693">
									

<p>To dogpile on to the discussion at hand&#8230;</p>
<p>The wiki has always held the phrase 'There is no canon' as pretty much the byline. Yes, this conflicts with most of the foundation writing, but half the point of the D-class contest is the fact that monthly terminations make no sense, and should be explained. That was the whole premise.</p>
<p>There's no retcon here, 'cause there's no con to ret. Every article is, within itself, the Prime Canon. Every article trumps every other article within itself. This skip says terminations are a skip. Therefore it is.</p>
<p>You are, of course, free to vote however you wish, but if preserving canon is your motivation, I think you might be off the mark.</p>

